  "level": 0,
  "ordinal": 0,
  "summary": "IEA gives tighter oil\nIn today's Oil Market Report (OMR), the International Energy Agency (IEA) provided a revised outlook that suggested a tighter oil market than orginally assumed, with rising demand estimates pushing against a decline in OPEC output. Indeed, with OPEC crude production having remained well above 31 mbpd during the first three quarters of 2012, global supply outpaced demand by 1.4 mbpd during that period. Those comfortable inventory builds are coming to an end for the moment, however, as the agency has hiked its oil demand forecasts, citing more rapid growth in Chinese oil demand.",
